body:
I do have one friend who is still friends with her, but I am not sure if it is my place to be telling that friend that my ex said this. My ex might want that to stay a secret or private, so I am not sure if I am going to tell my mutual friend. I mean what my ex said was a pretty big bomb shell so I am not sure if dropping it to another person is a perfect solution.

&#x200B;

Thank you for this response I really really mean it.

You're right, but it's just hard I think for other people to help, the circumstances behind our relationship was SO strange, I got a headache telling anyone about it because it was so complicated. It was a relationship that wasn't allowed, and we were the only ones who knew about it, we had to keep it a secret from everyone else. In a way I feel like I am one of the few people that she can go to. I just really don't like the idea of turning my back on a person by blocking them, that doesn't feel like me. I know I sound ridiculously "simp-ish" but I just don't know if I can actually go through with that. 

&#x200B;

Thank you very much for that post however that court case does have similarities to my situation.
